      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This would be a major plus for all group instances, including group public. Not only could it be used for the initial setup of group events, but it could also be used to delist/close down instances when the event is over without kicking people out. Basically allowing the instance to close down naturally since it would no longer show up in the instance list for new joiners. \n\nI would support the option of a delist or hidden toggle that instance owners or group moderators could toggle during instance creation and after the instance is already running. It should simply hide the instance from the instance listings.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-07-02T00:30:17.999Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "For many events, users are accustomed to having friends+ where if all users in that instance are on orange/red, the event is functionally \"not open\", allowing preparation beforehand.\n\nGroups+ instances are immediately joinable regardless of the status of anyone, including the instance creator, if you are a member of the group.\n\nIt would be nice to have a way to prevent anyone from joining while we're prepping. Perhaps a toggle or system to lock/unlock the instance from being joined?",
